Now js/game.js — the main game logic. This is big, so I need to keep it within reasonable size — maybe split into two files. Let me plan the code carefully, then write it in one go but keep it tight. If it's too big, split.

Structure:

```js
// State
const SAVE_KEY = 'pm_save_v1';
const DEFAULT_SAVE = { stars: {}, coins: 0, xp: 0, quizBest: 0, seenIntro: false };
let save = loadSave();
const TOTAL_LEVELS = 12;

// Ranks
const RANKS = [
  { xp: 0, name: '프롬프트 입문자', emoji: '🌱' },
  { xp: 200, name: '프롬프트 견습생', emoji: '🌿' },
  { xp: 450, name: '프롬프트 실력자', emoji: '⚡' },
  { xp: 750, name: '프롬프트 고수', emoji: '🔥' },
  { xp: 1050, name: '프롬프트 장인', emoji: '💎' },
  { xp: 1400, name: '프롬프트 마스터', emoji: '👑' },
];

// DOM helpers $, $$
// Screen switching showScreen(name)
// HUD update
// Title screen: speech bubble rotation messages
// Map render
// Level play: current level object, selections {}, stage switching
// buildPromptScore() => sum of slot scores + followup score
// AI response typing
// Followup options
// Result modal: stars, xp, coins, unlock collection
// Confetti
// Quiz mode
// Collection render
// Guidebook render
// Background particle canvas
```

Level flow: 
- startLevel(levelId): find level, fill situation texts, reset selections, go stage-situation, showScreen('screen-level').
- Clicking options: select per slot, toggle Selected class, update progress (filled count/5), enable send when all 5.
- btn-send: SoundFX.send, compute score tier, showScreen same, stage-answer, type response text (based on computed slotTotal: max 100 from 5 slots; tier: >=80 great, >=50 good else bad), then show followup panel.
- Followup option click: mark correct/wrong, add score (full slotTotal + followup option score 0/5/10/20 → total max 120), then after 700ms show result modal.
- Result: compute stars: total>=95 → 3, >=65 → 2 else 1. XP: stars*100; coins: stars*30 (+ first clear bonus?). Save. Modal with stars animation, confetti if 3 stars.
- modal-btn-next: next level or back to map.
- Retry: restart level.

Quiz:
- start: reset score, combo, time=60, shuffle questions, show play, interval 100ms decrement, render question, option click: correct → score += 100 + combo*20, combo++, coins; wrong → combo=0. Next question after 350ms. End: save best, add coins, show result screen.

Collection:
- Grid of 12 cards: locked if no stars. Click unlocked → detail modal with modelPrompt, why, copy button.

Guidebook:
- Render element cards, chips (click to copy), tips list.

Background canvas: floating particles (dots + Korean chars ㅎ ㅂ ㄷ?) subtle. Simple: ~40 dots drifting upward with twinkle. Confetti canvas: burst particles on 3 stars/fanfare.

Speech bubble: rotate messages on title screen every 4s.

Toast helper.

Also need total XP for HUD + title stats (cleared count, 도감 count).

First-visit: playSound on first interaction (unlock audio).

Let me write it — I'll keep it around 550 lines. Split into two files if needed: game.js (core) — I'll just write one file but be efficient.

